        <mxCell id="n32" value="METHOD &amp; PROOF (sketch): C1(N)=12N²+10N+50 cyc (bubble ≈ N²/2 compare-swaps, code-calibrated) → N=15: 2900 cyc = 17.06 µs · U = 17.06/100 + 2.85/1000 + 4.71/10000 = 17.39% ≤ 100% (Liu–Layland, harmonic set) OK · DMA occupies the link, not the CPU: τ2, τ3 execute during acquisition, CVB starts once its arm data is in · Shared single SPI: Tpath = 2N·3.6 + C1(N)/170 ≤ 100 µs → N=12: 97.56 PASS, N=13: 106.59 FAIL ⇒ Nmax = 12 · Dual SPI (one bus per arm): Tpath = N·3.6 + C1(N)/170 → N=19: 95.29 PASS, N=20: 101.71 FAIL ⇒ Nmax = 19 · Blocking-comm variant: U = 125% &gt; 100% FAIL — the green block alone decides feasibility" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F7F7F7;strokeColor=#8A8A8A;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=12;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;arcSize=16;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
